        .TITLE  DPDRIVER - DaynaPORT SCSI transport for OpenVMS VAX
        .IDENT  /V0.62/
;
; Copyright (c) 2026.
;
; Early bring-up SCSI class driver for the DaynaPORT SCSI/Link protocol.
; V0.62 is the native-PCSI packaging release.  It keeps the V0.61 packet-I/O
; implementation unchanged: SETMODE/SENSEMODE port lifecycle, serialized
; cloned-port requests, process-context buffered receive completion, and
; preservation of the executive's R6--R11 across direct and forked STARTIO.
; When assembled with DP$TCPIP_ALIAS defined, the same implementation exposes
; an XQA0:/QE0 compatibility name for TCP/IP Services while still addressing
; DaynaPORT target 4, LUN 0.  It does not emulate DELQA hardware.
; DP$VCI_FRONTEND adds a privileged, reversible public-VCI discovery frontend.
; An exact private SETMODE|CTRL request can install or remove three wrappers
; only while the LAN callback table and all driver queues match a closed-state
; contract.  Its exact XQA create/delete paths reach the clone lifecycle only
; after an ordinary STARTIO request has cached the hardware address.  The clone
; carries typed asynchronous VCRP
; ownership, SCSI-backed port management, bounded VCI transmit coalescing, and a
; timer-paced persistent receive path whose TQE runs only while a port is active.
; When transmit and receive work are both pending, the controller alternates
; them so sustained TCP traffic cannot starve inbound acknowledgements.  Each
; nonempty receive also requests one immediate follow-up READ, draining bursts
; to empty without increasing the idle 10-ms poll rate.
; The rejected post-WRITE holdoff experiment is removed.  Passive ICMP echo
; request/reply telemetry now distinguishes an upper transmit, successful SCSI
; completion, lower receive, and VCI delivery without changing packet handling.
; The first DaynaPORT command remains deferred until STARTIO.  OpenVMS VAX
; V7.3 does not provide a resumable SPI command context to a class driver's
; UNIT_INIT routine.  It also reconstructs the shared-controller register from
; the UCB after SPI resumption; the port contract restores R3, but not R6.  The
; template UCB is now marked UCB$M_TEMPLATE so SYS$ASSIGN can create protocol
; ports through DP_CLONED_UCB.  It deliberately remains DC$_MISC without the
; LAN-common DPT flags: this is a self-contained public-QIO implementation,
; not a client of the private CSMACD common layer.
;
; Device numbering follows the OpenVMS SCSI class-driver convention:
;
;       DPA<n0m>:       n = target ID, m = LUN
;
; Thus DPA400: connects to target 4, LUN 0 on PKA0.
;
; QIO interface:
;
;       IO$_AVAILABLE   enable the DaynaPORT interface
;       IO$_DEACCESS    disable the DaynaPORT interface
;       IO$_SETMODE     configure/start/stop an Ethernet protocol port
;       IO$_SENSEMODE   return LAN port characteristics and attributes
;       IO$_READPBLK    receive one Ethernet-format LAN payload
;       IO$_READLBLK    same as IO$_READPBLK
;       IO$_READVBLK    same as IO$_READPBLK
;       IO$_WRITEPBLK   transmit one Ethernet frame
;       IO$_WRITELBLK   same as IO$_WRITEPBLK
;       IO$_WRITEVBLK   same as IO$_WRITEPBLK
;
; This source uses the documented OpenVMS SCSI Port Interface macros and the
; standard driver macros supplied by SYS$LIBRARY:LIB.MLB on OpenVMS VAX V7.3.
; It must not be loaded on a production system before assembly/link review and
; static inspection of the generated map file.
;

        $CRBDEF
        $DDBDEF
        $DEVDEF
        $DYNDEF
        $FKBDEF
        $IODEF
        $IPLDEF
        $IRPDEF
        $NMADEF
        $PCBDEF
        $PRVDEF
        $SCDRPDEF
        $SSDEF
        $UCBDEF
        $VECDEF

.IF DEFINED DP$VCI_FRONTEND
        $DCBEDEF
        $VCIBDEF
        $VCRPDEF
        .LIBRARY /SYS$LIBRARY:LANUDEF.MLB/
        $LANUDEF
        $LDCDEF
        $LILDEF
        $TQEDEF
        $VCIBDLLDEF
        $VCRPLANDEF
.ENDC

P1                      = 0
